data srv3_host_lan_endpoint_note: String = "srv3's HOST OS endpoint, absent from this topology until 2026-07-24 — only srv3_bmc_endpoint (192.168.1.192) was modeled, so the model could name srv3's out-of-band controller but not the machine itself. Observed live from the operator's DHCP table (192.168.1.221, MAC 48:21:0B:81:C7:1D) and confirmed addressable by probe (sshd answers on :22). NOT yet workflow-reachable: the fleet-automation-ssh-key is authorized for no user tried (briansrls / ubuntu / root / installserver all refuse publickey), which is the B2 runner-user + A1 secret-materialization gap in gunbc.plans.fleet_subsumption_manual_gaps, not a networking fact. LEASE STATUS: as of 2026-07-24 the operator converted this to a STATIC reservation (192.168.1.221 ↔ MAC 48:21:0B:81:C7:1D), so the literal is now a fact rather than a lease-lifetime observation — matching the srv1/srv2 hosts and the srv1/srv2/srv3 BMCs. STILL DYNAMIC and therefore provisional: srv4's host (192.168.1.196) and srv4's BMC (192.168.1.195); those two literals remain only as stable as their leases until the operator reserves them. The DHCP-reservation act itself is an unmodeled manual step — a static-lease intent (MAC ↔ address binding on the operator's router) has no carrier here yet; see gunbc.plans.fleet_subsumption_manual_gaps for where that gap is tracked."

data srv3_host_lan_endpoint: NetworkEndpoint = NetworkEndpoint {
  label: "srv3-host-lan",
  host: Present { value: operator_host_srv3 },
  address: "192.168.1.221",
  role: HostOperatingSystem,
  locality: Lan,
}

